    "end": "They've been there since June.",
    "caption": "Those two by the sign won't be long.\n\nClasp: 5.6 million people, a 24-hour day, no moons, and hugs that last exactly as long as you've been apart. Back from the shops: a squeeze. Back from a fortnight away: a fortnight. Gap years are planned very carefully, and airports have benches for the people waiting to be let go of. Zoe went travelling for a year. Her mum got to the airport an hour early, with flowers.\n\n(On Earth, a study of athletes at the 2008 Olympics timed the average hug at about three seconds. On Clasp, that means you nipped out for milk.)\n\nShort trip or long hug?"
  },
